    "knowledge_point": "Completing a Table of Signs",
    "problem": "What are the missing entries in the sign table below?\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-5)$ | $(-5,1)$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+5$ | $-$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ |\n| $x-1$ | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ |\n| $(x+5)(x-1)$ | $+$ | {{field-3}} | $+$ |",
    "worked_solution": "On the interval $(-5,1),$ we can choose a test point ${x}_{1}=0.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5 & =0+5=(+), \\\\ x-1 & =0-1=(-), \\\\ (x+5)(x-1) & =(+)\\times (-)=(-),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we fill in the table as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-5)$ | $(-5,1)$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+5$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-1$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $(x+5)(x-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |",
