    "reasoning": "All 20 fields agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-80135: matching coefficients gives tan(phi)=1, so phi=45 degrees. q-107574: the amplitude is sqrt(5+4)=3 and the phase is arctan(2/sqrt(5)), approximately 0.730 radians. q-17128: (2 cos(3pi/2),2 sin(3pi/2))=(0,-2); the solution's second reference to the x-coordinate is a harmless typo. q-120598: the diagram selects the clockwise reflex angle, giving B an angle of 240-195=45 degrees and coordinates (sqrt(2),sqrt(2)). q-8683: the roots are pi/4 and -pi/4, with product -pi^2/16. q-72838: with alpha=arccos(4/7), the product alpha(2pi-alpha) rounds to 5.1. Both sign tables have middle-column signs +,-,-. q-115426: x(x+13) is negative between -13 and 0. q-27068: (x+2)(x-5) is positive outside its roots. q-27071: 3(x+3)(x-4) is nonpositive on [-3,4]. q-116200: (x+5)(x-2) is nonnegative outside its roots, including endpoints. q-74653: division by 3i gives -2/3-(5/3)i. q-7175: s(t)=5-10/t gives speed 10/t^2=2.5 cm/s at t=2. q-72252: the captured solution supplies center (-2,-2) and semiaxes 3 and 4, which yield the selected equation; the supplied image alone lacks readable coordinate labels, so its dimensions cannot independently be verified. q-115308: comparison with the translated ellipse form gives center (-2,3). No prior submitted answer or grade was supplied; MA evidence here consists exclusively of captured worked solutions.",
